From 3ea84fa3164a608f4a8b2e27ac4d153b0a80dec7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin <backcountrymountains@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 08:34:09 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Convert Dolby Vision profile 7 to 8.1 with libdovi on the
 DV decoder

Profile 7 (UHD Blu-ray) files only show their HDR10 base layer on the
Dolby Vision decoder. Configure the decoder as DvheSt, drop the
enhancement layer (NAL 63) and convert each RPU (NAL 62) to profile 8.1
with libdovi mode 2, as Kodi does. When a DV track ends up on a plain
HEVC decoder, strip NAL 62/63 so it plays as HDR10.

libdovi is reached through a small JNI shim (libdoviconv.so).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
